<title>HUNGARY: BA TO FLY JAGUAR EX-BUDAPEST TO AUSTRALIA.</title>
<headline>BA TO FLY JAGUAR EX-BUDAPEST TO AUSTRALIA.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways PLC (BA) plans at the end of August to transport a female jaguar from Budapest to Melbourne, the airline's Budapest office told Reuters on Friday.</p>
<p>The jaguar, a seven-year-old named Cili which now lives at Budapest Zoo, will leave on one of BA's two daily scheduled flights to London, BA cargo executive Monika Nagy said.</p>
<p>BA will transfer the animal onto a scheduled flight non-stop to Melbourne on a Boeing B747, Nagy added.</p>
<p>&quot;We can offer a good connection to Melbourne,&quot; she said. &quot;Cili can leave London the same day she arrives from Budapest.&quot;</p>
<p>BA arranged the shipment with the Budapest office of freight forwarder JAS Cargoways, Nagy said.</p>
<p>-- Ryan Tutak, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
